Title: "Differentiation and Integration"
Id: "5c64e9bc-323f-470e-b56b-3812afd2a703"


Text: "Differential calculus quantifies the instantaneous rate of change of a
       function, while integral calculus formalizes the accumulation of
       quantities and area. The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus establishes that
       differentiation and integration are inverse processes."
Id: "e33f5272-051b-41b6-af7f-e193d1108154"


SectionTitle: "Differentiation"
Id: "d3e7ecb7-d361-4548-bbd1-4cf6cee3a2b5"


[\derivative:of{f}:at{x0}]
Defines: d is \real
when:
. x0 is \\anything
. f is \\anything
expresses:
. forAll: epsilon is \real
  where: epsilon \:real.greater?:/ \real.zero
  then:
  . exists: delta is \real
    suchThat:
    . delta \:real.greater?:/ \real.zero
    . forAll: h is \real
      where:
      . h != \real.zero
      . \real.abs(h) \:real.less?:/ delta
      then: \real.abs(((f(x0 \.real.+./ h) \.real.-./ f(x0)) \.real.div./ h) \.real.-./ d) \:real.less?:/ epsilon
Documented:
. called: "derivative of $f?$ at $x0?$"
. written: "f?'(x0?)"
. description: "The derivative
                $f'(x_0) = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(x_0 + h) - f(x_0)}{h}$."
Id: "a8704cca-424a-4f17-a321-d5c3725e2090"


[\(differentiable)::real.function:on{U}]
Refines: f
when: U \:subset:/ \reals
specifies: f is \function:on{U}:to{\reals}
satisfies:
. forAll: x0 "in" U
  then:
  . exists: d is \real
    suchThat: d = \derivative:of{f}:at{x0}
Documented:
. adjective: "differentiable"
. description: "A function is differentiable on $U$ if its derivative exists at
                every point of $U$."
Id: "bddc1b83-707b-40f9-9b7f-c03513735f35"


SectionTitle: "The Mean Value Theorem"
Id: "20b85fa7-bbfb-4518-b953-1ee73f9b3eb3"


[\mean.value.theorem]
Theorem:
given:
. a, b is \real
. f is \function:on{\reals}:to{\reals}
where:
. a \:real.less?:/ b
then:
. exists: c is \real
  suchThat:
  . a \:real.less?:/ c
  . c \:real.less?:/ b
  . f(b) \.real.-./ f(a) = (\derivative:of{f}:at{c}) \.real.*./ (b \.real.-./ a)
Documented:
. called: "Mean Value Theorem"
. description: "For differentiable $f$, there is a point $c \in (a, b)$ where
                the instantaneous rate of change equals the average rate of
                change."
Id: "31c0c6c3-b04e-48c3-b6b3-37990aa819cd"


SectionTitle: "Riemann Integration and the Fundamental Theorem"
Id: "d60a18d3-c041-4705-9663-6c5e3f2c31ab"


[\riemann.integral:of{f}:on{a, b}]
Defines: I is \real
when:
. a, b is \real
. f is \function:on{\reals}:to{\reals}
Documented:
. called: "Riemann integral of $f?$ on $[a?, b?]$"
. written: "\int_{a?}^{b?} f?(x) \, dx"
. description: "The definite Riemann integral $\int_a^b f(x) dx$."
Id: "06b220c2-ee50-4d69-8de7-c1cbbd81e3bb"


[\fundamental.theorem.of.calculus]
Theorem:
given:
. a, b is \real
. f, F is \function:on{\reals}:to{\reals}
where:
. a \:real.less?:/ b
. forAll: x is \real
  then: \derivative:of{F}:at{x} = f(x)
then: \riemann.integral:of{f}:on{a, b} = F(b) \.real.-./ F(a)
Documented:
. called: "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
. description: "If $F$ is an antiderivative of continuous $f$, then
                $\int_a^b f(x) dx = F(b) - F(a)$."
Id: "17d7c6be-11d7-44bf-b522-515557063ed7"
